-- 1129: Blog post — "Power Apps and Power Automate with Copilot in Singapore: WSQ Course, Applied Skills and Funding"
--
--       Lead-in post for WSQ - Create Intelligent Power Apps and Power Automate Workflows with Copilot (TGS-2023036648).
--       Backdated to 2025-10-07 (published, status 1). No LinkedIn / Facebook share is
--       performed: linkedin_urn carries the manual-skip sentinel and the post ships
--       already-published, so publishDue never picks it up.
--
-- Every figure below was read off the LIVE course page on 2026-08-26, not invented:
--   * Fee card: full $1,600.00, GST $144.00 (9%), baseline nett $944.00
--     (SG/PR 21+, 50%), MCES/SME nett $624.00 (SG 40+, 70%).
--   * Course information: 4 days / 32 hrs, Beginner to Intermediate, 2 hrs assessment.
--   * Funding validity 18 Aug 2023 - 17 Aug 2027; Absentee Payroll $4.50/hr.
--   * Skills Framework: Applications Integration (ICT-DIT-3003-1.1).
--   * Exam weightings from the official study guide, skills measured as of Aug 2026.
--   * No exam-specific practice-exam URL exists, so the post links only the portal root
--     (never a deep link that 404s).
--
-- Notes for future editors:
--  * apply.php splits statements on ";" at end-of-line — the content HTML below is ONE line.
--  * Idempotent: WHERE NOT EXISTS on url_key, INSERT IGNORE on tag links. Safe to re-run.
--  * SG-only guard via @mms_instance — the CTA course is SG WSQ, absent on MY/GH.
--  * hero_image_url is NOT set here (SQL cannot render one) — generate on prod post-deploy.

SET @is_sg := IF(@mms_instance = 'SG', 1, 0);

INSERT INTO `mmd_blog_post` (`title`, `url_key`, `excerpt`, `content`, `author`, `status`, `published_at`, `related_skus`, `source_sku`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `meta_keywords`, `linkedin_urn`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) SELECT 'Power Apps and Power Automate with Copilot in Singapore: WSQ Course, Applied Skills and Funding', 'power-apps-power-automate-copilot-singapore-wsq-guide', 'PL-7001/7002/7003 is the Microsoft credential for business and IT staff building apps and workflows with Copilot assistance. This guide walks the exam domains and their weightings, sets out exactly what you pay after WSQ funding &mdash; $944 nett, or $624 for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above &mdash; and shows what the 4 days course covers.', '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p><strong>PL-7001/7002/7003</strong> is the Microsoft credential for business and IT staff building apps and workflows with Copilot assistance. This guide covers what the exam measures, what the 4 days WSQ course covers, and what you pay after SkillsFuture funding &mdash; <strong>$944</strong> for Singapore Citizens and PRs aged 21 and above, or <strong>$624</strong> for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above.</p></div><h2>Why PL-7001/7002/7003 is worth sitting</h2><p>Copilot changed the economics of low-code work. Describing an app in a sentence and getting a working first draft removes the blank-page problem that stopped most citizen developers before they started. This course covers building real canvas apps, model-driven apps and automated flows with Copilot in the loop, then making them production-worthy.</p><ul><li><strong>Copilot is used throughout</strong> &mdash; in Power Apps, Power Automate and Power Pages &mdash; rather than treated as a bolt-on.</li><li><strong>All three build surfaces are covered</strong>: canvas apps, model-driven apps with Dataverse, and automated flows.</li><li><strong>It maps to Microsoft Applied Skills credentials</strong> (APL-7001, APL-7002 and APL-7003), which are assessed as interactive labs rather than multiple-choice exams.</li><li><strong>Practical for immediate use</strong> &mdash; most participants leave with something they can deploy at work.</li></ul><p>The course is mapped to the Skills Framework under <strong>Applications Integration</strong> (TSC code ICT-DIT-3003-1.1), and leads to roles such as Power Apps Developer, Business Process Automation Specialist, AI Solutions Architect, Power Platform Consultant. <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-create-intelligent-power-apps-and-power-automate-workflows-with-copilot.html">Check the funding you qualify for</a>.</p><h2>The PL-7001/7002/7003 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><td>Credentials</td><td>APL-7001, APL-7002 and APL-7003 (Microsoft Applied Skills)</td></tr><tr><td>Format</td><td>Interactive lab assessment, not a multiple-choice exam</td></tr><tr><td>Weightings</td><td>Applied Skills publish a task list, not percentage weightings</td></tr><tr><td>Note</td><td>A 72-hour wait applies between lab attempts</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>PL-7001/7002/7003 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>These are Microsoft <em>Applied Skills</em> credentials, assessed in an interactive lab rather than a multiple-choice exam, so Microsoft publishes a task list rather than percentage weightings.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Skills measured</th><th>Weighting</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>APL-7001 &mdash; Create and manage canvas apps with Power Apps</td><td>Lab assessment</td></tr><tr><td>APL-7002 &mdash; Create and manage automated processes by using Power Automate</td><td>Lab assessment</td></tr><tr><td>APL-7003 &mdash; Create and manage model-driven apps with Power Apps and Dataverse</td><td>Lab assessment</td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Source: official Microsoft study guide, skills measured as of Aug 2026.</em></p><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>The 4 days (32 hrs) <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-create-intelligent-power-apps-and-power-automate-workflows-with-copilot.html"><strong>WSQ - Create Intelligent Power Apps and Power Automate Workflows with Copilot</strong></a> course is pitched at <strong>Beginner to Intermediate</strong> level and is delivered in our Woodlands classroom with hands-on labs, followed by a 2 hrs assessment. The outline tracks the official objectives:</p><ol><li>LU1 Get started with Copilot for Microsoft Power Platform</li><li>LU2 Create and manage canvas apps with Power Apps (PL-7001)</li><li>LU3 Create and manage automated processes by using Power Automate (PL-7002)</li><li>LU4 Create and manage model-driven apps with Power Apps and Dataverse (PL-7003)</li></ol><h2>Practise before you book the exam</h2><p>Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/practice-exams">Practice Exam Portal</a>, which carries timed mock papers across the Microsoft certification track. Rehearsing under exam conditions is the single best predictor of a first-time pass.</p><h2>What you actually pay: funding for PL-7001/7002/7003 training</h2><p>The full fee is $1,600 before GST. As an SWDA-funded WSQ course, the subsidy depends on your citizenship, age and who is sponsoring you:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Who you are</th><th>Subsidy</th><th>You pay (incl. GST)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Non-funded / international participants</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>$1,744</td></tr><tr><td>Singapore Citizen or PR, aged 21 and above</td><td>50%</td><td><strong>$944</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Singapore Citizen aged 40 and above (MCES), or SME-sponsored</td><td>70%</td><td><strong>$624</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>GST of $144 is charged at 9% on the full course fee of $1,600, as required for SWDA-funded courses &mdash; the subsidy applies to the course fee, not the tax.</em></p><p>Funding for this course is valid from <strong>18 Aug 2023</strong> to <strong>17 Aug 2027</strong>. You must register and complete the course within that window to qualify.</p><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">1. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Singaporeans aged 25 and above have an opening SkillsFuture Credit of $500 plus any top-ups, and those aged 40 and above received a $4,000 Mid-Career top-up. Credit can offset the fee payable after subsidy, though the Mid-Career top-up cannot be used on this course. <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/how-to-claim-skillsfuture-credit.html">How to claim SkillsFuture Credit</a>.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">2. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible employers can draw on SFEC to cover out-of-pocket costs when sponsoring staff. See our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/sfec.html">SFEC guide</a> for who qualifies and how to claim.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">3. PSEA</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Singapore Citizens can use Post-Secondary Education Account funds to offset the fee payable after subsidy. This course carries the PSEA tag, so it is eligible.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">4. UTAP</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>NTUC members can claim 50% of the unfunded fee under UTAP, capped at $250 a year, or $500 a year for members aged 40 and above. See the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/utap.html">UTAP guide</a>.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">5. Absentee Payroll</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Employers sponsoring staff can claim Absentee Payroll at $4.50 an hour, capped at $100,000 per enterprise per year, for the hours staff spend in training.</p></div></details></div><p><a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-create-intelligent-power-apps-and-power-automate-workflows-with-copilot.html"><strong>See the live fee breakdown for your profile &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Register for the 4 days WSQ course.</strong> Pick an intake on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-create-intelligent-power-apps-and-power-automate-workflows-with-copilot.html">course page</a> and apply your funding at checkout.</li><li><strong>Attend and complete the assessment.</strong> You need at least 75% attendance and a pass in the 2 hrs assessment to receive your WSQ Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Rehearse on the practice exams</strong> until you are consistently clearing the pass mark under timed conditions.</li><li><strong>Book and sit PL-7001/7002/7003</strong> as an Applied Skills lab assessment on Microsoft Learn. The certification exam is booked and paid for separately from the course.</li></ol><h2>Where to go after PL-7001/7002/7003</h2><p>Developers who want to extend the platform with code should look at <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-platform-developer-pl-400.html">PL-400</a>. For a certification that formally covers Copilot Studio agents, <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-platform-fundamentals-pl-900.html">PL-900</a> added that domain in its July 2026 update. Browse the full <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/microsoft-certifications-exams.html">Microsoft certification course catalogue</a> to plan the next rung.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is there an exam for this course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Not a traditional one. The related Microsoft credentials &mdash; APL-7001, APL-7002 and APL-7003 &mdash; are Applied Skills assessments taken as interactive labs on Microsoft Learn, not multiple-choice exams. The course itself leads to a WSQ Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need coding experience?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course is pitched at beginner-to-intermediate level and is built around low-code development with Copilot assistance.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Which credential covers the Copilot content?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>The Applied Skills credentials cover the Power Apps and Power Automate build skills. Copilot Studio agents are formally certified in PL-900, which added that domain in July 2026.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>4 days (32 hours), followed by a 2-hour assessment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What funding is available?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Singapore Citizens and PRs aged 21 and above get 50% subsidy, rising to 70% for Citizens aged 40 and above, plus SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for Power Apps and Power Automate with Copilot training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-create-intelligent-power-apps-and-power-automate-workflows-with-copilot.html"><strong>WSQ - Create Intelligent Power Apps and Power Automate Workflows with Copilot</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>', 'Tertiary Infotech Academy', 1, '2025-10-07', 'TGS-2023036648', 'TGS-2023036648', 'Power Apps and Power Automate with Copilot Singapore | WSQ Funded Course', 'Train for PL-7001/7002/7003 Power Apps and Power Automate with Copilot in Singapore. 4 days WSQ course from $624 nett after funding, full exam domain breakdown.', 'pl-7001/7002/7003 course singapore, power apps and power automate with copilot certification, pl-7001/7002/7003 exam, wsq microsoft course, skillsfuture microsoft certification, microsoft certification singapore, pl-7001/7002/7003 funding, pl-7001/7002/7003 training singapore', 'manual-skip-no-share', '2025-10-07 09:00:00', '2025-10-07 09:00:00' FROM DUAL WHERE @is_sg > 0 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `mmd_blog_post` WHERE `url_key` = 'power-apps-power-automate-copilot-singapore-wsq-guide');

